      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet, IC2.B2 is labeled EN but has no wire; IC2.A2 VIN is connected to NET0043.",
      "expected": "EN should be tied to VIN/NET0043 so the regulator is enabled whenever input power is present.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "IC2 FAN53610AUC33X: B2 EN; A2 VIN connects to NET0043. EthernetAndPower sheet, page 4/4."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "EN is hard-wired to VIN, so the regulator is always enabled whenever input power is present."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With EN floating, the 3.3 V regulator may remain disabled or behave unpredictably, preventing the board from powering up reliably.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["S2", "U8"],
      "pins": ["S2.2", "U8.48", "U8.45"],
      "nets": ["NET0015", "NET0014"],
      "observed": "The switch's pin 2 is connected to NET0015, which connects to U8.GPIO0; U8.HW_RESET is on the separate NET0014. The switch therefore does not operate HW_RESET as specified.",
      "expected": "The switch should connect its pin 2 to HW_RESET, with pin 1 connected to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "S2 pin 2 → NET0015; U8 pin 48 GPIO0 → NET0015; U8 pin 45 HW_RESET → NET0014. SkylabModule and EthernetAndPower sheets, pages 2/4 and 4/4."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "S1.1→GND, S1.2→HW_RESET (SKW92A pin 45)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Operating the slide switch can pull GPIO0 low instead of asserting hardware reset, so the intended reset control is unavailable and GPIO0 may be disturbed.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing shows the regulator enable pin left unconnected and the slide switch routed to GPIO0 rather than HW_RESET. Both differ from the specified design and can impair power-up and reset behavior."
}

